# Line-ending policy.
#
# Batch files must stay CRLF: cmd.exe mis-parses some multi-line constructs
# (parenthesised `if` blocks) when a .cmd is LF-only, and tools/check_package.py
# asserts CRLF. Without this rule the working tree only gets CRLF by accident of
# the local core.autocrlf setting.
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# The runtime payload (schema + Lua) is copied verbatim into the Rime user
# directory, and the installer compares it by SHA-256. Pin it to LF in every
# checkout so a git clone and a release ZIP install byte-identical files.
*.lua text eol=lf
*.schema.yaml text eol=lf
